{"productId": "768f793f-3267-4e0e-a279-f6db951870df", "modelName": "M1100", "modelDescription": "More than 40 years ago, the Model 1100 forever changed the way American shooters viewed autoloading shotguns. It was the first autoloader to combine the repeat-shot versatility of early-century models with the sleek, modern lines and handling qualities of revered double barrels. The Remington Model 1100 has been a field-proved favorite ever since. Its superb balance, handling, durability and soft recoil from the gas-operated action are the foundation of the Remington autoloading legacy.The Competition Synthetic is super-tuned for the competitive scene. By overboring the 30\" barrel and lengthening the forcing cones, it has has improved shot-to-shot pattern consistency and made what was one of the softest-recoiling actions in the world even easier on your shoulder. The receiver and all internal parts feature a nickel-Teflon finish for the smoothest, most reliable cycling ever. It's optimized for 2 3/4\" target loads and light field loads, and the barrel has a 10mm target-style rib. All these, plus a host of other upgrades, transform an already legendary design into an unstoppable force at the range.", "manufacturerName": "Remington", "subProducts": [{"isFirearm": true, "isNfa": false, "subProductId": "25963da1-a694-422c-b73d-72d86cbde0f5", "description": "Remington, 1100 Sporting, Semi-automatic, 410 Gauge, 3\" Chamber, 27\" Barrel, Polish Blued, Walnut Stock, Right Hand, 1 Choke, 4 Round ", "imageUrls": ["https://main-images.gearfire.com/SubProductImages/be1ec5fc-9611-4e8f-af18-4eed388602d1"], "isDefault": false, "manufacturerPartNumber": "R29549", "upc": "810070680039", "attributes": [{"attributeNameId": "571a5bce-61b6-44f6-bf8a-15fc76aa270a", "attributeName": "Color", "attributeValueId": "58c2cd8d-c3f1-4094-8c03-69c1f29bb1f1", "valueName": "Brown"}, {"attributeNameId": "4a6c7638-340d-4690-94ee-c5c30501e3bf", "attributeName": "Hand", "attributeValueId": "e0166eaf-76d9-4